{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Go now, see the welfare of your brothers.</b> And נא is nothing but language of request. Even though every day I hear tidings from them, it is the way of the world that you should go there yourself, for they are your brothers." "<b>And the welfare of the flock.</b> This teaches that a person should inquire after the welfare of something from which he derives benefit." "<b>And he sent him from the valley of Hevron.</b> The city sits on a mountain, and Jacob escorted him to the valley. And so our Rabbis said: Jacob escorted Joseph, and they were engaged in the passage of the broken-necked heifer, and from there he sent him."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:07:41.585256975Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}